AUDIO ASSET PROVENANCE

apps/orcastra/voice_data.c contains a synthesised singing voice. The melody is
"Daisy Bell" (1892), which is in the public domain. The audio itself is
generated entirely from a source-filter model — a buzzy clipped-saw excitation
through three formant resonators — and no part of any recording was sampled,
processed or included. Every other sound in this project (drums, synth
waveforms, the reverb and delay tanks, the sampler's seed content) is likewise
synthesised at build time or on the device.
